  hook: 'A god comes home to the city of his birth and is refused. He does not argue. He arranges the conditions in which the city\'s young king dresses himself in women\'s clothes, climbs a mountain to spy on the rites he has banned, and is torn apart by his own mother. The Bacchae is the strangest play in the Greek tragic corpus and the one no one has fully agreed about for two and a half thousand years.',
